        <member name="T:Gordic.Security.WebService.CscController">
            <summary>
            Provides endpoints for handling authorization code flow in PKCE-based authentication.
            </summary>
            <remarks>This controller is responsible for receiving and validating authorization codes and their
            associated state parameters during the PKCE (Proof Key for Code Exchange) authentication process. It ensures
            that the state parameter is valid and updates the associated PKCE information upon successful
            validation.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Gordic.Security.WebService.CscController.GetAuthorizationCode(System.String)">
            <summary>
            Retrieves an authorization code associated with the specified state.
            </summary>
            <remarks>This endpoint is part of the PKCE (Proof Key for Code Exchange) flow. The
            authorization code is removed from the cache  after it is retrieved to ensure it can only be used once.
            Clients should continue polling if the code is not yet available.</remarks>
            <param name="state">The unique state identifier used to retrieve the authorization code. Cannot be null, empty, or whitespace.</param>
            <returns>An HTTP response containing the authorization code if it exists and is valid.  Returns <see
            cref="T:System.Web.Http.Results.NotFoundResult"/> if the code is not available, or  <see
            cref="T:System.Web.Http.Results.BadRequestResult"/> if the <paramref name="state"/> parameter is invalid.</returns>
        </member>
